\section{Computing Generalizable Variables by Variance}

For a relaxed value restriction, the checker can calculate which
variables in an expansive initializer's type occur only covariantly.
Assume a sound ML-like variance discipline, with independently
verified constructor variances, and a finite inferred monotype.
Read each constructor's parameter polarity, multiply it by the
polarity of the surrounding position, and join all occurrences of
each variable. Represent signs by sets of $+$ and $-$, treating
invariant positions as the set of both signs. In this small
implementation every parameter is variant or invariant; phantom
parameters are not represented. The result is a set of variable
identities still eligible after excluding those free in the
environment.

\begin{sudocode}
  \Input result type $T$, environment free variables $F$
  \Output eligible variables for an expansive right-hand side
  \State $P\gets$ map with empty sign sets
  \Procedure{Visit}{$X,s$}
    \If{$X$ is a variable}
      \State $P[X]\gets P[X]\cup s$
      \Comment{Combine every occurrence}
    \Else
      \ForAll{child $Y$ with declared signs $q$}
        \State \Call{Visit}{$Y,s\cdot q$}
        \Comment{A domain flips the sign}
      \EndFor
    \EndIf
  \EndProcedure
  \State \Call{Visit}{$T,\{+\}$}
  \State \Return $\{a : P[a]=\{+\},\ a\notin F\}$
\end{sudocode}

Suppose a factory call produces
$\mathsf{List}(\alpha)\times(\beta\to\beta)
\times\mathsf{Ref}(\mathsf{List}(\gamma))$.
The pair positions and list element positions are positive.
The two $\beta$ occurrences contribute opposite signs through
the arrow, and the reference contributes both signs to $\gamma$
despite the inner list. With an empty environment free set, the
algorithm generalizes just $\alpha$. Two uses can instantiate
the list element at $\mathsf{Bool}$ and $\mathsf{Int}$, but a use
that fixes the shared $\gamma$ to $\mathsf{Bool}$ prevents a later
use from treating the same reference's contents as integers.
This conservative rule leaves $\beta$ monomorphic even if the
particular factory always returns an identity function.

The traversal invariant is that each sign summarizes the access
positions on its path from the root. A double contravariant
path contributes a positive occurrence. Do not count only the
first visit to a shared type node: that node can be reached
with opposite signs. A memo table for pairs of nodes and sign
sets bounds the work by a constant multiple of the size of an
acyclic type graph. The traversal implements only the eligibility
test; declared variance, environment exclusion, and the soundness
of the language's relaxation are separate obligations.
